  "final_output": "# Deployment Rollback Procedure\n\n## Preconditions\n\n- The database migration is backward-compatible; do **not** reverse it during this rollback.\n- You have access to deployment, traffic-management, and monitoring systems.\n- Record the rollback start time and notify the incident channel.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. **Establish a baseline**\n   - Confirm the current application version and identify the previous stable version.\n   - Record the current request volume, latency, and error rate.\n   - Verify that error-rate monitoring is available throughout the rollback.\n\n2. **Drain traffic**\n   - Stop routing new traffic to the deployment instances.\n   - Allow active requests to complete.\n   - Confirm that traffic to those instances has reached zero or the approved drain threshold.\n   - **Do not begin the rollback until traffic is drained.**\n\n3. **Roll back the application**\n   - Deploy the previous stable application version.\n   - Leave the backward-compatible database migration in place.\n   - Keep traffic disabled while startup and health checks run.\n\n4. **Validate before restoring traffic**\n   - Confirm that all instances are healthy.\n   - Run the required smoke tests.\n   - Check logs for startup, database, and dependency errors.\n\n5. **Restore traffic gradually**\n   - Route a small percentage of traffic to the rolled-back version.\n   - Monitor request volume, latency, and error rate.\n   - Increase traffic in stages only while metrics remain healthy.\n\n6. **Enforce the stop condition**\n   - **Immediately stop the rollback and stop increasing traffic if the error rate rises above 2%.**\n   - Remove traffic from unhealthy instances if safe to do so.\n   - Preserve logs and metrics, notify the incident commander, and escalate for investigation.\n   - Do not continue without explicit incident-command approval.\n\n7. **Complete the rollback**\n   - After all traffic is restored, continue monitoring through the required observation period.\n   - Confirm that the error rate remains at or below 2%.\n   - Document the deployed version, retained database migration, metrics, timestamps, and any issues.\n   - Notify stakeholders that the rollback is complete.",
